In article <883@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu> arrom@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu (Ken Arromdee (600.429)) writes:

>Now that everyone is finished with dogs, here's another query: 3.0 is going
>to have more different monsters, including succubi and incubi.  What should
>they do?

The purpose of succubi and incubi is the begetting of half-human/half-demon
creatures. Hence, they look only for the fittest and most powerful of humans,
so you shouldn't see them until pretty late in the game.

They take special pleasure in corrupting those who are good, so knights and
priests are more likely to see them. Allowing oneself to be seduced by a
succubus or incubus would cause these characters to fall into disfavor with the
gods.

Naturally, if you are the Hand of Elbereth, they will have no dealings with
you, unless you have somehow managed to displease the gods. The favorites of
the gods are *NOT* considered fair game for demons.

Intelligence is important. They might not mess with cave men.

I seem to remember that there will be new stats in 3.0, including charisma.
High charisma would definitely make one more attractive to succubi and incubi.

The initial attack would be one of seduction, rather than violence. If the
seduction is successful, all your possessions will be in a heap on the floor.
The creature should probably whisk you away to some more comfortable setting
during the interlude. When you return to your old location, there's no telling
what might be waiting for you. Your dog might have gone wild, your goods might
have been stolen, etc.

If the seduction fails, then the succubus or incubus would revert to a normal
attack. It would probably fight like a regular demon, but succubi might have
less physical damage, and poison you instead. Each succubus or incubus should
have one special ability (poison, fire, freezing, teleportation, etc.) which
could be generated at random.

After a successful seduction by an incubus, a female character would be in no
further danger from him. But, a succubus could try to kill a male character
when she was through with him. He might get a few rounds (enough time to get
his armor and weapon) after his return before she shows up and comes after him.
Or, we could say that she's off in Hell gestating. The young develop fast!

A female character, if pregnant, would quickly outgrow her armor, unless it was
of some soft type. For a short time, she would have to do without her main
armor, although helmet, shield, boots, gloves, and cape would be allowed. Her
dexterity might be reduced, and she would have to eat more. When she delivers,
a pair of demons arrive and try to carry the child off to Hell. If she slays
them, she'll have a demon-child, which will act as a pet, and grow to full
demon-hood very quickly. To avoid all this nastiness, we could say that she
conceives and delivers instantly, and the child is stolen away from her before
she is returned from Hell to the dungeon.

When you arrive in Hell, your demonic offspring is waiting for you. It has been
specially trained to kill you at all costs. It has everything that you have,
only better. +1 on each stat, +1 level, +1 on each piece of armor and each
weapon. It may also have a special attacks, which would reflect the nature of
the demon parent. Of course, if you kill it, you get lots of nice equipment! I
wouldn't give it all the spells, spell books, wands, etc.

Killing your demon offspring will restore you to favor with the gods.
